  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Image Emphasis",
    "long_instructions": "# Image Emphasis with Hover\r\n\r\nNot only can we use the `hover` pseudo-class to draw a user's attention to a hyperlink on our page, but we can also it to **style other elements too**!\r\n\r\nLet's see how we can code our images with the \"hover\" pseudo-class to bring attention to them.\r\n\r\n# Do This\r\n\r\n**In the CSS file:**\r\n1. Add a rule set to style the images with the \"hover\" pseudo-class. \r\n   - Add the following properties:\r\n      - Increased width of the image\r\n      - \"fushia\" border color\r\n      - A defined `border-width` to at least 10px\r\n   - Add any other properties you think will make the image stand out and bring a user's attention to it!\r\n3. Hover over the the images to see what happens!\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/e19b6fd29ec3cad6dd2a99669ff8a145-image-1707950878809.gif\">",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Learn how to use the \"hover\" pseudo-class to bring a user's attention to an image!",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/b94276893ae107d7b2bc6a900627c778-imageHover.gif",
    "submittable": "false",
