        "21": {
          "id": "21",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    \n    <!-- Title -->\n    <h1>Mystical Creatures and Where to Find Them</h1>\n    \n    <!-- info content -->\n    <p>Embark on a mythical journey and uncover the secrets of creatures from legends around the world. From the depths of the ocean where the Kraken lurks to the forests home to the elusive Bigfoot, click on each image to discover the stories that have captivated human imagination for centuries.</p>\n    \n    <!-- hyperlinked image gallery -->\n    <div class=\"images\">\n      <a href=\"bigfoot.html\"><img src=\"bigfoot.jpg\" alt=\"bigfoot\"></a>\n      <a href=\"kraken.html\"><img src=\"kraken.png\" alt=\"kraken\"></a>\n      <a href=\"phoenix.html\"><img src=\"phoenix.png\" alt=\"a phoenix\"></a>\n      <a href=\"dragon.html\"><img src=\"dragon.png\" alt=\"dragon\"></a>\n      <a href=\"griffin.html\"><img src=\"griffin.png\" alt=\"griffin\"></a>\n      <a href=\"unicorn.html\"><img src=\"unicorn.png\" alt=\"unicorn\"></a>\n    </div>\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  </body>\n</html>",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "22": {
          "id": "22",
          "name": "unicorn-tapestry.jpg",
          "contents": "",
          "folderId": "0",
          "url": "/level_starter_assets/CSD%20U2L18-L9b_2025-v2/uuid/74cba2f3-915e-4d41-839e-c53e46cf7fdc.jpg",
          "type": "starter",
          "active": false
        },
        "23": {
          "id": "23",
          "name": "unicorn.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n\n    <a class=\"back-link\" href=\"index.html\">Back to Mystical Creatures</a>\n\n    <h1>Unicorn</h1>\n\n    <div class=\"page-image\">\n      <img src=\"unicorn-tapestry.jpg\" alt=\"A medieval tapestry depicting a white unicorn defending itself from hunters and dogs\">\n    </div>\n\n    <p>The unicorn is a legendary creature usually depicted as a horse-like animal with a single, long, spiraled horn growing from its forehead. Across many cultures, the unicorn has come to symbolize purity, grace, and untamed wildness.</p>\n\n    <p>Stories about horned, horse-like creatures date back thousands of years, with early written descriptions appearing in ancient Greek accounts of natural history, which described unicorns as if they were real animals living in India. Throughout the Middle Ages, the unicorn became especially popular in European art and literature, often appearing in tapestries and manuscripts as a rare, almost sacred creature that could only be captured or tamed by a pure-hearted maiden.</p>\n\n    <p>The tapestry above, woven in the late 1400s, is part of a famous series called the Unicorn Tapestries, which depict a dramatic hunt for the creature. Scenes like this one reflect just how seriously the unicorn was treated in medieval Europe, not just as a myth, but as a symbol woven into art, religion, and storytelling for centuries.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"citation\">\n      <p>\"The Unicorn Defends Itself,\" South Netherlandish tapestry, 1495–1505. The Cloisters, The Metropolitan Museum of Art, Gift of John D. Rockefeller Jr., 1937. Public domain, via <a href=\"https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/467640\">The Met</a></p>\n    </div>\n\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
